SELinux namespace lifecycle selftests
=====================================

Build and run from a configured kernel tree:

  make -C tools/testing/selftests/selinuxns
  make -C tools/testing/selftests TARGETS=selinuxns run_tests

For a source tree whose exported headers have not been staged yet:

  make headers_install INSTALL_HDR_PATH=/tmp/selinuxns-headers
  make -C tools/testing/selftests/selinuxns \
       CFLAGS="-Wall -Wextra -Werror -O2 -isystem /tmp/selinuxns-headers/include"

The lifecycle test skips operations unavailable because of kernel support,
SELinux policy, host-init CAP_SYS_ADMIN, or nsfs file-handle permissions.  To
exercise successful setns(fd, 0), launch it single-threaded with an already
active SELinux namespace FD inherited at SELINUXNS_ACTIVE_FD.  The test does
not require or invoke CRIU.
